    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just what the textbooks say. science is always catching up to what people feel intuitively. if the sequence isn't just 'chemical instructions' but actually follows a specific mathematical architecture, then traditional biology would miss it because they aren't looking for higher-order patterns. i'm not saying it defies physics, i'm saying it might be the bridge between biology and mathematics. if we look at the non-coding regions, the parts they call 'junk DNA,' wouldn't it be possible that those patterns are where the real blueprint is hidden? can we at least try to look at the mathematical possibilities?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
